 ## Unreleased — candidate Pack 1.1.0
 
+- H8-SKILL-R1 remediation (unreleased candidate; nothing is published, tagged, or installed by this change): `rdk-model-zoo/scripts/read_catalog.py` default discovery now also probes the unified per-platform layouts `docs/release/{x5,s,x3}/models.yaml` and the frozen `platforms/{platform}/...` snapshots, preferring the active unified manifest over the same platform's snapshot — consistent with `inspect_repo.py`. Discovery stays local to the script (no sibling-skill or repository import), so single-skill flat installs remain self-contained. Explicit `--manifest` selection and the historic flat single-platform layouts are preserved: exactly one candidate is still selected implicitly, multiple candidates fail with `ambiguous-manifest` plus the actionable `manifest_candidates` path list and are never narrowed by branch, filename, or the S group, and missing manifests remain `manifest-not-found` (unknown). Implicitly or explicitly selecting a `platforms/` snapshot is disclosed with a warning.
+- Entry member `rdk-model-zoo` advances 1.1.1 → 1.1.2 for that behavior change (pack.json, SKILL.md frontmatter, governance card, pack README, structural test expectation). The Pack stays candidate 1.1.0 with `release_state: unreleased-candidate`. Per the governance card's change-review rule, one eval definition (`zoo-eval-013`, unified multi-platform lookup without a selected target) is added to expose the former default-invocation false absence; it is a behavior definition only, not an executed Agent result.
+- This fixes the recorded default-invocation failure on the unified checkout (`docs/releases/unified-migration/2026-09-28-skill-catalog-layout-review.md`, finding H8-SKILL-R1: documented `read_catalog.py --repo <unified checkout>` returned rc=2 `manifest-not-found` although the active unified manifests exist). Codex independently reviews this remediation; the whole H8 item is not closed by it.
 - Integrate the upstream rdk_x5 increment (commit `d1b24f65`, "fix(skills): align Model Zoo routes with current OE workspaces (#175)") into this migration adaptation: OE workspace paths `.drobotics-x5/` and `.drobotics-s/` replace the retired `.drobotics/`/`.horizon/` names, the S-series router handoff becomes `drobotics-router`, and the S deployment-workflow source link points to `D-Robotics/oe-skills-s` tag `v1.1.0` instead of the retired `rdk-skills` path. Upstream declares Pack 1.0.1 released; that state describes the upstream pack — this branch's adapted candidate remains unpublished and untagged.
 - Member versions absorb the increment without regressing earlier local levels: entry `rdk-model-zoo` 1.1.0 → 1.1.1 (matches upstream), `rdk-model-zoo-repo/develop/validate/review` 1.1.0 → 1.1.1 (the Q5 1.1.0 feature level is preserved; upstream's 1.0.1 is not adopted as a downgrade), `rdk-model-zoo-integrate/release` 1.0.0 → 1.0.1 (matches upstream). The Pack version advances 1.0.0 → 1.1.0 as a candidate because the tree now contains 1.1.x members, and `release_state` stays `unreleased-candidate`.
 - Governance cards now restate the real member versions: the Q5 step had left the repo/develop/validate/review cards at 1.0.0 while `pack.json`/SKILL.md frontmatter said 1.1.0; this inconsistency is corrected as part of version self-consistency.
